Moi the barbarian fared well. XL16, had just reached Medusa level,
finished the quest, Sokoban and the mines.
He had a quite average equipment, (no wish of any kind available), so
a +4 dwarven mithril coat, a rusty +3 helmet and a +5 blessed
longsword, a ring of teleport control along with a few goodies. Lots
of bags of holding, too.

However, for some reason, Moi had angered his god, the mighty Crom,
and his bare AC was back to 10. I thus decided to go Leprechaun
hunting in order to get some money to pay the nice priestess of Crom
on DLvl10 and to buy some divine protection.
There was a nifty Leprechaun room on DLvl 25. So I went there and
struck one of them, having all my gold hidden in the BoH. Suddenly, a
monster appears out of nowhere. The leprechaun had a wand of create
monster. He processed to create things like a mind flayer, which I
soon blessed-genocide with my single saved genocide scroll. Then came
an arch lich. The net result was a level with an arch lich and a titan
(damn things), a minotaur, a dragon, giants, rothes, trolls, ettins
and whatnots.
This sounded like a real challenge. I zapped myself with a /oT, moved
to the stairs, and killed the lich. Then, monsters surrounded me. I
got up, dipped a scroll of earth in holy water, went down, read the
scroll, and proceeded to kill the dragon, ettin, etc, making
occasional retreats upstairs to kill the rock troll that followed me
and to heal. Finally, I got all the monsters behind their boulders.
Hidden behind my fort, I then zapped at the purple worm and gremlins
behind the wall, teleported to kill the titan and back to the stairs.
I had killed all the monsters to the left of the fort (which totally
prevented monsters from coming from the right of the level).

This felt great.
Surely I would ascend soon.

An elf lord whose corpse lay beneath a boulder provided me with a pick
axe, so I crushed a few boulders to loot what was beneath and make way
for the stairs down. Suddenly, the lurking Minotaur appeared. Had
something dug a passage south of the boulder fort? I'll never know.
So I struck it. I had 154 hit points. I strike. When I'm ready for my
next move, I'm down to 98. Eeek. That hurt. But well, thinks the brave
barbarian. He can't deal 98 hits in one blow can he?
I strike the minotaur again. Next, checking my hit points, I see a
nice 0. Nearby, I see the ominous word: Fainted. And now dead.
The damn fight took so long that I starved and I was so focused on the
fight I didn't realise it, just to be killed by the minotaur.

All this because of a lousy leprechaun and its wand of create monster.

Arghh... Oh, well, it could be worse, I could have been finished by a
newt.

